I does probably make sense to say a little more about the project review
process, which seems to work well enough at weeding out things which
don't have broader support.

Of course, the definition of 'very narrow' is highly open to
interpretation, as a quick glance at last year's approved projects
shows.  So perhaps 'deemed useful to a significant constituency of R
users' would be more correct? I'm aiming at allowing/encouraging 'domain
specifc' proposals from large R constituencies such as HPC, biostats or
finance, and being cautious of projects that seem like a chapter in a
narrow dissertation that (almost) no one is likely to read.

