On 03/24/2012 03:29 AM, Christoph Molnar wrote:
> Hello everyone,
>
> I have a project idea.
> There is no package for Wikipedia articles. That surprised me, because one could do a lot
> of interesting statistical analysis with Wikipedia's content,  for example do text mining
> on the articles using the tm package or analyze the backlinks, plot wordclouds and so on.
>
> The package should contain a function which provides a convenient way for retrieving whole
> Wikipedia articles. The user puts the topics as strings in and gets the articles as output.
> This could happen via different sources. One would be online using the official Wikipedia
> API (http://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php).
> This source would need the RCurl and XML package.
> Another source could be the Wikipedia xml dump files. They contain all of the articles
> which results in pretty huge files (2.5GB). I think one does not want to use R for parsing
> such an amount of data. The solution could be to use an external program or import the
> dump into a SQL table and read it with R using the RMySQL package.
>
> An article could be stored as a S4-object. Other formats like S3 or a simple list would
> also be possible.
>
> The package should in addition provide some functions for preparing the articles for text
> mining and other statistical analysis.
> I would also add some functions for a first explorative analysis, like summary and plot
> methods.
>
> What do possible mentors think about this project idea? Is this interesting enough for the
> R community?
> I'm also interested in the image labels project.
> It would be great to hear your thoughts about my proposal, so that I can decide on which
> to focus on.
>
> If you like the project idea, do you want to be my mentor?
>
> Best regards
> Christoph Molnar
>
>
>
>

